# UST.G3BL H11 Proof-Prime Initializer No-Go Theorem

## Result

The good-reduction place `(11,gamma-3)` used to certify G3BI smoothness and
compile the G3BK correction is not an admissible H11 transport initializer at
the root-containing endpoint `a=1`. This is an exact statement about the
finite Macaulay/de Rham presentation. It is not a singularity statement about
the characteristic-zero endpoint or its geometry.

## Determinant-Lemma Core

Let `A` be the frozen square B89 H11 coordinate chart. Its columns consist of
the quotient units and the selected original-Jacobian columns, and its
invertibility over `GF(11)` is already certified. Let `U V^T` be the endpoint
correction restricted to the 1,186 active selected columns. The exact
coordinate solver computes `A^-1 U`, so the matrix determinant lemma reduces
the endpoint chart to

```text
L = I_1186 + V^T A^-1 U.
```

Exact Gaussian elimination gives

```text
rank_GF(11)(L) = 1185,
det_GF(11)(L)  = 0.
```

Thus the selected `5439 x 5439` endpoint chart has rank `5438`, with one
missing direction.

## Exhausting The Available Columns

The selected chart omits 1,071 original-Jacobian columns from the complete
H11 Macaulay presentation. G3BL reconstructs their endpoint values using the
same G3BI correction, solves all 1,071 columns in the certified B89 chart, and
evaluates them against the exact left-null functional of `L`.

The result is

```text
unused columns tested:                  1071
nonzero left-null evaluations:             0
rank of full 5439 x 6510 presentation: 5438
```

Therefore no column swap inside this complete presentation repairs the
endpoint chart at this proof place. The obstruction is not an artifact of one
unlucky selected minor: the entire available H11 augmented presentation has
corank one over `GF(11)`.

## Interpretation

This separates two facts that must not be conflated:

1. G3BI proves that the selected characteristic-zero eta9 member is smooth by
   proper smooth good reduction at `(11,gamma-3)`.
2. G3BL proves that the auxiliary H11 Macaulay/de Rham presentation loses one
   rank at the same special-fiber endpoint.

Smoothness of the variety does not force every chosen cohomology presentation
to remain a basis after reduction. The correct consequence is therefore an
initializer change, not rejection of G3BI or of the G3BJ path.

The G3BK transcendental-interior argument is unaffected. Every interior
parameter is transcendental, whereas every frozen-chart pole is algebraic.
Only the endpoint initializer must be supplied at an alternate split good
prime or directly in characteristic zero.

## Claim Boundary

G3BL does not prove:

- singularity of the H11 characteristic-zero endpoint;
- singularity of the G3BI geometric member;
- failure of H11 transport at every good prime;
- the corresponding H02 endpoint status;
- a characteristic-zero H11 inverse action; or
- integral transport and the terminal 248-row readout.

